# `SEQUENCE-CONTAINMENT-SCOPE`: `in=` on ALL FIVE acceptors — message, operand, lifeline,
# state and fragment — in one valid document, so the acceptor list is pinned by
# a model golden and not only by its error messages. Every one is sense 1, *the
# element this one lives inside*, and every value is a fragment or an operand
# id.
#
# The `lifeline in=` line is the rare one and it is here on purpose: it says a
# participant exists only inside a fragment. It is also the acceptor with no
# use in any authored figure, so this fixture is its only demonstrator.
figdown 0.4 sequence
title "Every acceptor of in="
lifeline c "Client"
lifeline s "Server"
fragment outer "attempt" type=opt
operand a1 "if reachable" in=outer
lifeline probe "Probe" in=a1
message c -> s "request" in=a1
state c "WAITING" in=a1
fragment inner "retry" type=loop in=a1
operand b1 "while no reply" in=inner
message c -> probe "poll" in=b1
message c <- probe "still waiting" in=b1
